    {
      "term": "Unsupervised domain adaptation",
      "definition": "Unsupervised domain adaptation is a method where a model is trained to perform well on a set of data without having any training labels available in the target domain. The goal is to leverage labeled source data to improve performance on unlabeled target data.",
